WEBVTT

01:29.980 --> 01:33.230
<b>Contact Tamacity
Emon Bank</b>

01:43.870 --> 01:48.620
<b>Valentine's Fair</b>

01:52.460 --> 01:55.630
<b>Valentine's
Anime Collab</b>

01:55.890 --> 01:57.490
Valentine's...

01:58.590 --> 02:01.830
Wonder if they have anything
cute but not too pricey.

02:04.280 --> 02:08.140
I guess I'll get a box with
lots in it for all the staff.

02:09.230 --> 02:10.760
This one looks tasty.

02:14.420 --> 02:15.740
This is all Blue gets.

02:16.150 --> 02:19.290
Red is technically our leader.

02:19.290 --> 02:21.450
Better get him something decent.

02:25.830 --> 02:28.290
<b>No sense of direction whatsoever</b>

02:28.490 --> 02:30.410
Would this be a little mean?

02:39.890 --> 02:41.490
I'll go with the safe choice.

02:41.920 --> 02:44.630
I don't want to hear whatever
snarky comment Blue would have.

02:45.240 --> 02:49.490
Next, something grown-up
and stylish for Black.

02:52.490 --> 02:54.480
That just leaves the twins.

03:00.610 --> 03:01.200
Magical girl chocolate?!

03:01.200 --> 03:03.300
Magical Girl Angel Anima
Magical girl chocolate?!

03:03.300 --> 03:04.830
Magical Girl Angel Anima

03:05.070 --> 03:07.830
M-Must buy!

03:07.830 --> 03:10.860
I was going to buy something
for myself anyway!

03:16.220 --> 03:17.730
But which one?!

03:20.320 --> 03:23.640
Magical girls really are the cutest...

03:24.220 --> 03:26.330
Miss Magical Girl.

03:27.670 --> 03:34.000
Take care not to lose the things
you treasure, Miss Magical Girl.

03:44.430 --> 03:47.960
Too bad I can't gift him some chocolate, too.

03:48.540 --> 03:51.040
<b>Valentine's Day</b>

03:51.800 --> 03:53.550
Hold out your hand already.

03:53.550 --> 03:54.750
Huh?

03:54.750 --> 03:57.050
What, does your stomach hurt?

03:57.770 --> 03:59.700
Yeah, my "chronic colic."

03:59.700 --> 04:01.460
Poor you.

04:01.460 --> 04:02.590
Shove it.

04:04.090 --> 04:06.130
What? Chocolate?

04:06.130 --> 04:08.010
Oh, a Valentine.

04:08.010 --> 04:12.240
Hey, you'd better not be so stingy
with Red and the others.

04:12.240 --> 04:15.580
No, they're getting proper gifts in boxes.

04:15.580 --> 04:16.650
That's fine, then.

04:16.650 --> 04:17.770
What's it to you?

04:26.470 --> 04:29.920
She doesn't have to get me any
if it's that big of a deal.

04:30.750 --> 04:33.880
Yet she hand-delivers some to everyone.

04:34.290 --> 04:36.830
She's conscientious about
the weirdest things.

04:49.300 --> 04:50.500
That's sweet.

04:52.290 --> 04:54.970
You know, I forgot to get a thank-you.

04:54.970 --> 04:56.540
What do we say?

04:57.740 --> 05:00.340
Nope, not cute in the slightest.

05:02.440 --> 05:05.740
<b>Contact Tamacity
Emon Bank</b>

05:05.740 --> 05:07.820
<b>White Day
Contact Tamacity
Emon Bank</b>

05:13.140 --> 05:15.890
What kind of chocolate
should we give in return?

05:15.890 --> 05:18.080
I've already made up my mind!

05:18.400 --> 05:19.560
What about you, Blue?

05:20.680 --> 05:21.930
I'm thinking about it.

05:24.590 --> 05:27.260
Then is it okay if we split up?

05:27.260 --> 05:28.220
Yeah!

05:29.370 --> 05:31.440
Don't wander into other stores!

05:31.770 --> 05:34.850
They say strawberry things are in this year.

05:34.850 --> 05:37.110
And so are baked sweets.

05:38.300 --> 05:39.490
Oh yeah?

05:39.490 --> 05:40.400
Let's go.

05:42.180 --> 05:44.440
Um, um...

05:44.440 --> 05:45.790
Where could it be?

05:49.730 --> 05:52.770
This is from that shop Black
said sells tasty stuff!

05:52.770 --> 05:53.950
That's the ticket!

05:53.950 --> 05:54.080
<b>Done already
That's the ticket!</b>

05:54.080 --> 05:55.990
<b>Done already</b>

05:55.990 --> 05:56.000
That's cute.
<b>Done already</b>

05:56.000 --> 05:57.820
That's cute.

05:57.820 --> 06:00.250
And it's a color Pink likes.

06:00.250 --> 06:00.360
<b>Done
already
And it's a color Pink likes.</b>

06:00.360 --> 06:02.460
<b>Done
already</b>

06:13.580 --> 06:17.490
Two hours of agonizing and you still
haven't made up your mind, Blue?

06:17.490 --> 06:18.600
Well...

06:19.330 --> 06:21.940
I think she'll complain
no matter what I pick.

06:22.980 --> 06:24.240
I'm so annoyed.

06:25.920 --> 06:31.350
Don't worry. We'll tell Pink you
couldn't stop thinking about her.

06:33.360 --> 06:36.010
Don't you <i>ever</i> tell her that!

06:36.340 --> 06:39.620
Well, we're going to go look for Red.

06:41.010 --> 06:43.910
Wait! Is he lost right now?

06:43.910 --> 06:45.100
I'll come with you!

06:51.760 --> 06:52.690
Huh?

06:52.970 --> 06:57.850
<b>Lost</b>

06:57.980 --> 07:03.980
<b>Mr. Villain's Day Off</b>

07:18.710 --> 07:22.640
When something makes me anxious,
it isn't long before my stomach hurts.

07:23.350 --> 07:26.370
I remember my mother giving
me something for it that day

07:26.370 --> 07:29.490
and me squeezing my brother's little hand.

07:32.880 --> 07:36.320
Our father was a Ranger,
and one day, he didn't come home.

07:37.130 --> 07:40.770
The man who appeared instead
was the darkest Ranger.

07:41.530 --> 07:45.540
That was the day I became
Ranger Sunrise Blue.

07:47.350 --> 07:50.220
The guy in black was Twilight Black.

07:51.720 --> 07:54.450
Genetics have nothing
to do with Ranger powers.

07:54.450 --> 07:57.230
When the previous generation goes,
their powers pass on.

07:58.270 --> 08:02.480
Ranger energy resonates and becomes
stronger the closer we are,

08:02.480 --> 08:05.160
so we live at the same base
as much as possible.

08:06.520 --> 08:08.960
He always looks sleepy.

08:08.960 --> 08:11.600
And the stuff he says is complicated.

08:12.730 --> 08:14.980
After that came Daybreak Pink.

08:15.570 --> 08:17.960
She's younger than me. And sassy.

08:19.400 --> 08:22.770
We got in a fight when she said
our hero suits were lame.

08:24.160 --> 08:26.400
Your glasses are what's lame.

08:27.310 --> 08:29.730
Black was always busy, day in and day out.

08:30.360 --> 08:35.130
When we talked to him about school,
he'd nod and nod off.

08:36.160 --> 08:37.360
A few years later...
And then...

08:37.360 --> 08:38.660
A few years later...

08:42.130 --> 08:43.590
They're so cute!

08:44.990 --> 08:46.240
Black.

08:46.240 --> 08:48.260
These two are the Green Ranger?

08:48.260 --> 08:50.230
Can't you tell by their energy?

08:50.230 --> 08:51.210
It's green.

08:51.210 --> 08:52.700
I was just making sure.

08:52.700 --> 08:54.190
They're babies.

08:54.190 --> 08:55.620
Can they fight?

08:55.620 --> 08:58.070
You're just a kid yourself.

08:58.070 --> 09:00.480
Not as much as you are.

09:00.480 --> 09:01.760
That's enough.

09:02.070 --> 09:05.510
These two are undeniably Aurora Green.

09:05.510 --> 09:06.990
Sora and Mugi.

09:07.350 --> 09:12.000
Their faces look the same,
but Sora is a girl and Mugi is a boy.

09:12.000 --> 09:13.180
So I'm told.

09:13.180 --> 09:16.520
Instead of "Green,"
can we call them by their names?

09:16.520 --> 09:18.570
We'll have to, since there's two of them.

09:19.560 --> 09:22.190
The energy from the twins is very weak.

09:23.100 --> 09:28.530
When you two are here, try to resonate
with them as much as you can.

09:28.530 --> 09:29.740
Okay.

09:30.900 --> 09:32.300
Hey, Black.

09:33.370 --> 09:36.910
I don't <i>have</i> to go to a regular school.

09:37.370 --> 09:39.880
They can teach me here, can't they?

09:39.880 --> 09:42.390
You dislike going to school that much?

09:42.390 --> 09:47.650
It's not that! Being here all the time would
make resonating and training easier.

09:50.520 --> 09:51.560
What?

09:51.960 --> 09:54.510
As one of the previous Rangers once said,

09:54.950 --> 09:58.620
"The only people here are adults
working with the Rangers.

09:59.090 --> 10:01.070
I want you to mingle with the outside world,

10:01.070 --> 10:03.800
with friends your own age,

10:03.800 --> 10:08.260
so you can appreciate for yourself
what it is we're trying to protect."

10:09.830 --> 10:12.270
Are you saying she's not my friend?

10:12.270 --> 10:13.140
What?!

10:13.140 --> 10:16.130
F-Friends?! With <i>you</i>?!

10:16.630 --> 10:17.580
You're not?

10:17.580 --> 10:18.730
No way!

10:20.630 --> 10:24.770
The Rangers and the staff here
are comrades who fight together.

10:25.030 --> 10:31.120
So we might be... a little different
than friends on the outside.

10:32.270 --> 10:33.810
Huh.

10:35.980 --> 10:37.950
Is Black asleep?

10:39.050 --> 10:40.720
Even though he was just talking?!

10:41.190 --> 10:42.960
Black, wake up!

10:42.960 --> 10:44.980
Go to bed already.

10:48.200 --> 10:49.420
They're not here.

10:53.120 --> 10:54.530
They're not here.

10:55.250 --> 10:58.750
Several months after that...

10:58.750 --> 10:58.760
Welcome back, Blue, Pink.
Several months after that...

10:58.760 --> 11:01.240
Welcome back, Blue, Pink.

11:01.240 --> 11:02.620
Thanks.

11:02.620 --> 11:04.000
Welcome home.

11:04.000 --> 11:06.390
What gives? Don't walk with me.

11:06.390 --> 11:07.590
Don't walk with <i>me</i>.

11:07.590 --> 11:10.140
I'm going to see Sora and Mugi.

11:10.140 --> 11:12.430
Would you mind not copying me?

11:15.790 --> 11:19.830
Every day, we went to school
and trained as Rangers.

11:19.830 --> 11:22.890
We also helped take care of Sora and Mugi.

11:23.620 --> 11:26.180
I even got to see my family on occasion.

11:26.830 --> 11:29.250
Black was always on patrol.

11:30.800 --> 11:32.870
Even though he's super nocturnal,

11:32.870 --> 11:35.970
he's also been looking
for Red lately during the day.

11:35.970 --> 11:38.210
Is Black going to be okay?

11:38.640 --> 11:41.520
I'm just glad the enemy's been quiet.

11:41.890 --> 11:46.140
If they made any serious moves right now,
we wouldn't stand a chance.

11:46.140 --> 11:48.910
We had better remained focused, too.

11:48.910 --> 11:49.600
Yes.

11:51.850 --> 11:52.990
We have a problem!

11:52.990 --> 11:55.810
Green is... The twins are missing!

12:12.000 --> 12:13.640
It was while I wasn't paying attention!

12:14.570 --> 12:16.820
There's no evidence of intruders!

12:16.820 --> 12:18.680
Check the security cameras!

12:19.110 --> 12:20.550
Sora!

12:20.550 --> 12:23.070
Mugi! Where are you?!

12:24.060 --> 12:25.950
Answer us!

12:26.850 --> 12:27.880
Oh!

12:27.880 --> 12:29.820
We're calling, but they <i>can't</i> answer us!

12:29.820 --> 12:31.040
They're babies!

12:31.040 --> 12:32.360
You're right!

12:33.140 --> 12:34.220
Dummy.

12:34.220 --> 12:35.880
What? Talking about yourself?

12:35.880 --> 12:36.560
Huh?!

12:36.810 --> 12:38.600
You know, you really...

12:41.480 --> 12:43.890
I'll search this way. Don't follow me.

12:53.430 --> 12:55.020
Hey!

12:55.020 --> 12:57.700
Are you still mad about what I said before?

12:58.190 --> 12:59.830
What you said before?

13:00.920 --> 13:03.640
That we're not friends.

13:03.640 --> 13:06.250
Oh. Not really.

13:06.760 --> 13:09.050
You always say nasty things.

13:11.060 --> 13:11.800
I...

13:12.700 --> 13:14.360
I...

13:16.580 --> 13:21.080
I'd be okay with us... <i>becoming</i> friends.

13:27.360 --> 13:28.610
I'll pass.

13:28.610 --> 13:30.110
Huh?!

13:30.750 --> 13:35.740
I have a little brother,
and you're kind of like a little sister.

13:35.740 --> 13:38.530
A-A little sister?

13:38.790 --> 13:42.870
When I think about it,
you feel more like a sister than a friend.

13:43.500 --> 13:47.750
I don't think we need to worry too
much about what Black said before.

13:47.750 --> 13:49.140
Besides, right now—

13:53.930 --> 13:55.110
That was...

13:55.110 --> 13:56.880
Green's energy!

13:58.890 --> 14:00.150
They're not here.

14:01.960 --> 14:03.230
They're not here.

14:04.180 --> 14:05.660
Mom...

14:05.660 --> 14:07.200
Dad...

14:07.200 --> 14:08.360
Where are you?

14:09.560 --> 14:10.860
They're not here.

14:11.160 --> 14:12.410
They're not here.

14:17.480 --> 14:18.620
They're not here...

14:20.040 --> 14:21.140
Sora!

14:21.140 --> 14:22.050
Mugi!

14:30.540 --> 14:32.790
They transformed and got bigger!

14:33.220 --> 14:35.000
There's only one of them now.

14:35.640 --> 14:38.070
Does that mean they combined?

14:38.070 --> 14:41.190
That's Sora and Mugi's energy, so probably.

14:41.800 --> 14:42.980
What?!

14:43.920 --> 14:47.700
Dad, Mom... Where are you?

14:52.940 --> 14:53.870
I'm sorry!

14:54.330 --> 14:57.550
Your mother and father are gone!

14:58.530 --> 14:59.490
Hey!

14:59.840 --> 15:00.860
But...

15:01.290 --> 15:07.130
We and everyone on staff promise
to raise you two as best we can!

15:08.550 --> 15:11.560
This isn't a sad or painful place to be.

15:12.430 --> 15:13.640
It'll be okay.

15:18.420 --> 15:19.360
Also...

15:19.770 --> 15:25.530
Let's see... Black is really cool.
The cafeteria food is good.

15:25.530 --> 15:26.580
And...

15:28.380 --> 15:32.790
W-We'll be your siblings!

15:34.060 --> 15:39.250
We can't be your mother and father,
but we'll be your brother and sister!

15:40.200 --> 15:42.700
We'll always be together!

15:48.790 --> 15:51.890
Always together?

16:04.940 --> 16:08.320
Then it won't be lonely.

16:40.340 --> 16:44.850
Winding up in a place like this
all of a sudden must have scared them.

16:46.510 --> 16:50.010
Why do you keep making
that face? It's creepy.

16:50.010 --> 16:51.080
Huh?

16:52.780 --> 16:57.160
It's because you said we're family.

16:57.160 --> 17:03.050
We can't be your mother and father,
but we'll be your brother and sister!

17:03.730 --> 17:06.920
You're the one who said
I was like your sister!

17:06.920 --> 17:08.210
That's true.

17:08.470 --> 17:12.350
But if we'll always be together,
does that mean Rangers for life?

17:12.750 --> 17:16.620
Except you don't really like
being a Ranger, do you?

17:20.890 --> 17:22.420
I don't.

17:22.420 --> 17:24.500
What I really want to be is...

17:24.960 --> 17:26.410
Is what?

17:29.880 --> 17:33.000
Why should I have to tell you?

17:33.000 --> 17:34.950
Huh? Why wouldn't you?

17:34.950 --> 17:35.940
Forget it.

17:35.940 --> 17:38.820
Oh, I really hate the hero suits.

17:38.820 --> 17:40.330
They're full-body tights.

17:41.530 --> 17:44.470
I think they're fine. Very Ranger-like.

17:44.470 --> 17:45.200
Huh?!

17:45.200 --> 17:45.950
Huh nothing!

17:48.280 --> 17:53.040
Either way, I don't dislike this place
or the people here.

18:00.660 --> 18:04.010
I forgot, but my stomach started hurting...

18:09.640 --> 18:12.310
I hear you two had a big day.

18:12.320 --> 18:12.930
<b>Dried Squid</b>

18:12.930 --> 18:15.020
Have some dried squid as a reward.
<b>Dried Squid</b>

18:15.020 --> 18:15.030
<b>Dried Squid</b>

18:15.440 --> 18:17.350
I'd rather have some cheese.

18:17.350 --> 18:19.170
Beef jerky for me.

18:20.420 --> 18:21.950
Take the squid or leave it.

18:25.330 --> 18:28.340
The reason Sora and Mugi's energy is weak

18:28.340 --> 18:31.740
is that they each have a half-share
of one Ranger's energy.

18:32.240 --> 18:33.380
Or so I was told.

18:33.960 --> 18:36.970
Do all twins combine when they transform?

18:37.680 --> 18:41.330
I don't know of any other twin
Rangers, so I can't say.

18:41.330 --> 18:42.730
Aww.

18:42.730 --> 18:45.730
Will we have a full team once we find Red?

18:46.280 --> 18:48.840
That's right. We're looking now.

18:48.840 --> 18:50.850
I wonder where they are.

18:51.290 --> 18:54.280
There's a chance they still haven't been born.

18:55.070 --> 18:57.150
What if they're lost somewhere?

18:57.400 --> 18:59.200
Of course they aren't.

19:00.320 --> 19:02.210
That would present a problem.

19:02.990 --> 19:05.290
My dad was a Ranger.

19:05.920 --> 19:09.210
I always thought he was cool.

19:09.580 --> 19:13.580
Though if you asked me if I'd wanted
to be one too, I couldn't have said.

19:14.730 --> 19:16.130
But I know one thing.

19:19.510 --> 19:23.140
I don't mind this place and its people either.

19:32.780 --> 19:33.910
What is it?

19:33.910 --> 19:36.170
We have a favor to ask.

19:36.170 --> 19:38.780
What do you say, Big Brother?

19:38.780 --> 19:40.260
Big Brother!

19:40.260 --> 19:42.410
Please, Big Brother!

19:42.410 --> 19:44.670
Big Brother!

19:46.010 --> 19:49.040
Whenever you call me that,
I know there's trouble.

19:49.040 --> 19:51.780
You won't even hear our request?

19:51.780 --> 19:53.080
Let's hear it!

19:53.080 --> 19:57.080
Hooray! Thanks, Big Brother!

19:58.750 --> 20:00.090
"Big Brother"?

20:01.610 --> 20:03.830
The four of you are siblings?!

20:03.830 --> 20:05.210
I had no idea!

20:07.740 --> 20:10.080
Only the two of us are related.

20:10.080 --> 20:11.250
Oh, really?

20:11.250 --> 20:12.040
Yeah.

20:12.500 --> 20:15.380
Stay just the way you are, Red.

20:17.680 --> 20:18.730
Okay!

20:23.950 --> 20:29.950
<b>Mr. Villain's Day Off
Mr. Villain's Day Off</b>

20:31.520 --> 20:34.620
It's been years since the
last generation of Rangers passed.

20:36.160 --> 20:38.370
As the only one left,

20:38.370 --> 20:42.670
I went on searching for the new Rangers
who inherited their powers.

20:56.150 --> 20:59.310
Dealing with kids, teaching rookies...

20:59.730 --> 21:01.400
I'm so not cut out for this.

21:02.190 --> 21:05.930
How did you guys teach me?

21:06.580 --> 21:08.780
Why was I the one who survived?

21:09.290 --> 21:10.610
What can I do...

21:12.620 --> 21:15.610
to make sure they lead long lives?

21:17.500 --> 21:18.620
Black!

21:24.190 --> 21:26.170
I'm truly not cut out for this.

21:40.140 --> 21:44.430
But I will<i> fulfill my duties as a Ranger.</i>

21:45.510 --> 21:47.500
So just you watch.

23:14.030 --> 23:20.000
<b>Mr. Villain's Day Off</b>

23:20.000 --> 23:20.710
<b>Mr. Villain's Day Off
MR. VILLAIN'S DAY OFF</b>

23:21.480 --> 23:24.930
What sound does the clockwork cat make?

23:25.590 --> 23:27.870
Schrödinger will not respond.

23:29.140 --> 23:31.480
A portrait in the vacant mirror.

23:32.010 --> 23:34.660
A red string trembles.

23:35.730 --> 23:38.530
When the paper vessel speaks.

23:40.140 --> 23:42.310
A blue bond forms.

23:43.520 --> 23:45.700
The afternoon of a faun.

23:46.890 --> 23:48.650
When the flowers scatter...

23:48.650 --> 23:49.940
<b>When the Flowers Scatter</b>
